          "content": "✅ Note: Facebook Lead Ads Integration (Window Revival)\n\nPurpose\nThis workflow pulls Lead Ads form submissions from Facebook for the business Page Window Revival and processes them in n8n (flatten fields + prevent duplicates + send to destination such as Google Sheets/CRM).\n\nKey IDs\n\nPage Name: Window Revival\nPage ID: 135479543431\nLead Form Name: Window Revival Lead Generation 2022\nForm ID: 624246452531250\nGraph Endpoint: /{FORM_ID}/leads\n\nRequired Permissions (must be granted on the token)\nleads_retrieval ✅ required\npages_show_list\npages_read_engagement\npages_manage_ads (recommended)\nads_management (sometimes needed depending on setup)\n\nImportant: The /leads endpoint must be called using a Page Access Token (Window Revival page token), not a plain user token.\nAPI Call Used\nGET leads for the form\nURL:\nhttps://graph.facebook.com/v25.0/624246452531250/leads\n\nQuery:\nfields=id,created_time,field_data\nlimit=25 (adjustable)\n\nRecommended auth method:\nUse header:\nAuthorization: Bearer <PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN>\n(avoid putting token in URL if possible)\nOutput Data Structure\n\nFacebook returns:\n\ndata[] list of leads\nEach lead has:\nid = lead id (unique submission id)\ncreated_time\nfield_data[] = array of objects with {name, values[]}\n\nExample keys in field_data:\nfirst_name, last_name, email, phone_number, etc.\nData Transform (Flatten)\nWe convert field_data[] into flat JSON so it’s easy to map into Sheets/CRM.\nFlatten result example:\n\nlead_id\ncreated_time\nfirst_name\nlast_name\nemail\nphone_number\nwhich_suburb?\nquantity\netc.\nDuplicate Prevention (Important)\n\nPolling will fetch older leads again.\nWe must deduplicate using lead_id.\n\nRecommended approach:\n\nStore each processed lead_id in n8n Data Store (or database)\n\nSkip leads whose lead_id already exists\n\nProduction Notes\nGraph API Explorer tokens can expire; use a stable Page token strategy for production.\nFor real-time leads (no polling), use Facebook Webhooks: subscribe the Page to leadgen.\n\nTroubleshooting\nError (#190) must be called with a Page Access Token\n→ You used a user token. Switch to Page token.\n\nError (#100) Tried accessing nonexistent field (leads)\n→ Wrong path like /me/leads. Use /FORM_ID/leads.\n\nEmpty data: []\n→ No new leads or token doesn’t have access to that Page/Form.\nWhich node should you use: Facebook Graph API node vs HTTP Request?\nBoth work — here’s what I recommend:\n\n✅ Best for reliability: HTTP Request\nYou control the exact endpoint and headers\nEasier debugging\nWorks consistently across n8n versions\n✅ Best for convenience: Facebook Graph API node\nNice UI, but can be confusing with Node/Edge setup\n\nMake sure Node = FORM_ID, Edge = leads\n\nIf your HTTP Request is working already, stick with it.",
          "height": 1888,
          "width": 1456
        },
